{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/522106-ghost-hunters","id":522106,"title":"Ghost Hunters","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-20T11:26:42-07:00","id":522106,"title":"Ghost Hunters","content":"Ah, by which I mean hunters who are ghosts, not hunters of ghosts.<br /> <br /> Anyway, considering the sorts of inflamed passions, emotional traumas, and singular obsessions the Vigil can produce, I imagine that deceased hunters leave behind restless echoes quite often. Has anyone done anything with the concept of hunting from beyond the grave?<br /> <br /> The rules for ephemeral beings make them kind of problematic for running as PCs, though there are certainly workarounds. Though converting most of Mummy: The Curse to 2e looks like a bit of a nightmare, the Lucid Dead Numen seems fairly portable as-is. The benefits of intangibility and in-built supernatural powers are balanced out by anchor concerns, plus the fact that not a small number of monsters have abilities that can just obliterate ghosts (primarily mages, Sin-Eaters, and mummies, but the occasional vampire or werewolf too for good measure).<br /> <br /> Perhaps there's even a Compact of unquiet shades who band together to take care of unfinished business. Maybe they have an Endowment that bestows the Anchor Condition on anything connected to the Vigil. Could be they're empowered by a Kerberos or Deathlord or something. Or maybe it's just a Ghostwalk-type scenario in which the more sentient ghosts out there handle the sorts of problems particular to undead existence.<br /> <br /> Could be something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T11:55:02-07:00","id":522153,"title":"","content":"you know how a group of ghosts and humans ho work together to investigate the Underworld and the Twilight is going to be called, right?.. <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Orpheus\" target=\"_blank\">right</a>?..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T12:07:17-07:00","id":522179,"title":"","content":"KSI-21 has Ghost recruits, most are probably unwilling but I'm sure they wouldn't say no to a loyal operative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T12:27:00-07:00","id":522231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/522106-ghost-hunters?p=522153#post522153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">you know how a group of ghosts and humans ho work together to investigate the Underworld and the Twilight is going to be called, right?.. <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Orpheus\" target=\"_blank\">right</a>?..</div> </div> </div> </div>Oui da, there is indeed Orpheus, as well as whatever Operation MNEMOSYNE might be, but the metaphysical/cosmological rift between OWoD ghosts and NWoD is quite broad. Seeing Orpheus Group in Hunter would be pretty cool though (although between Cheiron, Deva Corp, LDI, Hototogisu, and Utopia Now, conceptual space for another for-profit monster-hunting organization is beginning to grow thin).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">KSI-21 has Ghost recruits, most are probably unwilling but I'm sure they wouldn't say no to a loyal operative.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fair. I could see some groups being open to the idea of deceased members hunting with them, while others would be more averse. I would savor immensely the emotional drama of the ghosts of Long Night hunters trying to convince their living brethren that they're not demons (followed immediately, of course, with a Diabolus incursion).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T14:59:06-07:00","id":522572,"title":"","content":"You know that non-demonic ghosts do appear in the bible, the Witch of Endor - so a Long Night hunter wouldn't find it hard to imagine. Heck, they have that Merciful creed, they might even try to redeem actual demons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T18:11:28-07:00","id":522737,"title":"","content":"That's true yeah. Forgot about Endor. Anyway they were just the first example I thought of. Plus, no matter what a given group's party line might be, individual feelings are bound to come into play when dealing with dead friends, family, comrades, etc. Hmm. More ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}